orked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""] ["question-3bd80b9b-2655-5bf4-bdf9-f7428c6e7e13" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-99fd9b59-7583-550f-9b77-a9aef65a8d04" :answer-field/id #uuid "99fd9b59-7583-550f-9b77-a9aef65a8d04"] ["answer-01804a80-5ad0-5362-964c-9ececb6d064d" :answer/id #uuid "01804a80-5ad0-5362-964c-9ececb6d064d"] ["answer-01804a80-5ad0-5362-964c-9ececb6d064d" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-01804a80-5ad0-5362-964c-9ececb6d064d" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-3b8e51e4-40fa-57ba-90ff-180ebb919ccb" :answer/id #uuid "3b8e51e4-40fa-57ba-90ff-180ebb919ccb"] ["answer-3b8e51e4-40fa-57ba-90ff-180ebb919ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-3b8e51e4-40fa-57ba-90ff-180ebb919ccb" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-8405f8f8-e192-530e-9104-fc411cda42f6" :answer/id #uuid "8405f8f8-e192-530e-9104-fc411cda42f6"] ["answer-8405f8f8-e192-530e-9104-fc411cda42f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8405f8f8-e192-530e-9104-fc411cda42f6" :answer/value "I, II, and III"] ["answer-725de94a-3ee8-5f32-b2e7-5e74ed4217f0" :answer/id #uuid "725de94a-3ee8-5f32-b2e7-5e74ed4217f0"] ["answer-725de94a-3ee8-5f32-b2e7-5e74ed4217f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text] 